<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24063" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-sūmo</span></b> , mpsi, mptum, 3,
			v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to take for</i> any thing; hence <i>to
				apply to</i>, <i>expend upon.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<i>In aliquid</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut nullus teruncius insumatur in quemquam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 5, 17, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sumptum in aliquam rem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Inv. 2, 38, 113</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sestertios tricenos in cenam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 2, 24, 11</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			With <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paucos dies reficiendae classi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					2, 53</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(g).</b>
			With abl.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non est melius quo insumere possis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 2, 102</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>To apply</i>, <i>employ</i>, <i>bestow</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">operam frustra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					10, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">operam libellis accusatorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					3, 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitam versibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Or. 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			With <i>in</i> and abl.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec in evolvenda antiquitate satis operae
					insumitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. Or. 29</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(g).</b>
			With <i>ad</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnis cura ad speculandum hoc malum insumitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 46, 70, § 153</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To take to one</i>'<i>s self</i>, <i>to take</i>, <i>assume</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interficiendi domini animum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 14, 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medium latus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dignas insumite mentes Coeptibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 12, 643</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>To use up</i>, <i>exhaust</i>, <i>weaken</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 2, 2, 60</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corporis virtutem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Acut. 2, 37, 213</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
